solve agent configuration through different paths. Moving action orchestration to Electron must also remove React-side executable-command resolution.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_006_agent_command_sources.md:19:- Make persisted desktop config the single source of truth.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_006_agent_command_sources.md:26:- Changing supported agent configuration affects action runs and continuation immediately and after restart.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_006_agent_command_sources.md:29:- Tests cover both entry points and persisted config resolution.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_006_agent_command_sources.md:35:- `design\\feature_descriptions\\ready\\F_031_config_persistence.md`\ndesktop\\package.json:10:    \"package:windows\": \"electron-builder --config electron-builder.config.cjs --win nsis --x64\",\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:14:Still present after the F-033 agent-profile rework (2026-07-06 audit). The built-in profile list (`BUILTIN_AGENT_PROFILES` in `app/src/data/agent_profiles.ts` and its duplicate `desktop/agent_profiles.js`) contains `{ command: 'system', name: 'system' }`, and `buildAgentCommand`/`resolveAgentCommand` use the profile's `command` verbatim as the shell command. Selecting the `system` profile (app menu, action popup, action json or `desktop.agent` config) spawns a process literally named `system`, which fails — there is still no mapping to any real default agent.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:18:* remove the fake `system` built-in profile — user-defined profiles with free-form commands now cover the \"configurable agent string\" requirement, and `codex`/`claude` remain sensible defaults.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:23:* No selectable config value causes a spawn of a nonexistent literal command.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:24:* The agent command is configurable as text and used consistently by all agent execution paths.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:31:* `design\\feature_descriptions\\F_031_config_persistence.md`\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:538:    \"node_modules/@eslint/config-array\": {\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:540:      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@eslint/config-array/-/config-array-0.21.2.tgz\",\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:553:    \"node_modules/@eslint/config-helpers\": {\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:555:      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/@eslint/config-helpers/-/config-helpers-0.4.2.tgz\",\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:3987:        \"@eslint/config-array\": \"^0.21.2\",\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:3988:        \"@eslint/config-helpers\": \"^0.4.2\",\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:4113:        \"tsconfig-paths\": \"^3.15.0\"\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:7947:    \"node_modules/tsconfig-paths\": {\ndesktop\\package-lock.json:7949:      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/tsconfig-paths/-/tsconfig-paths-3.15.0.tgz\",\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_012_left_panel_layout.md:19:- Relocate `GithubAuthPanel` to a sensible home: the toolbar (account button/menu) or the project-open dialog (pairs with F-027/B-019).\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_012_left_panel_layout.md:25:- Auth is still reachable (toolbar or dialog) in both modes.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_015_electron_context_isolation.md:14:`desktop/main.js` creates the window with `contextIsolation: false, sandbox: false`, and `preload.js` assigns bridge objects (and its closure over Node modules like `child_process`, `fs`, git) directly onto `window`. The window loads a **configurable, remotely deployed URL** (J-001 design). Any compromise of that site — or of any dependency it ships — gains transitive access to shell execution and the filesystem. This is a real security defect, not a style preference.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_015_electron_context_isolation.md:24:- All existing bridge features (data, auth proxy, theme, config, actions) work unchanged through `contextBridge`.\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.js:30:function assertSigningIdentityIsConfigured(secrets) {\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.js:39:function createBuilderConfig(secrets = loadSigningSecrets()) {\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.js:40:    assertSigningIdentityIsConfigured(secrets);\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.js:105:    createBuilderConfig,\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:14:    createBuilderConfig,\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:17:} = require('./builder_config');\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:19:describe('electron-builder configuration', () => {\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:21:        const config = createBuilderConfig({ certificateSubjectName: 'Example Certificate' });\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:23:        expect(config).toMatchObject({\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:35:        expect(config.files).toContainEqual(expect.objectContaining({ from: '.', to: 'desktop' }));\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:36:        expect(config.files).toContainEqual(expect.objectContaining({ from: '../app/dist', to: 'desktop/renderer' }));\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:37:        expect(config.files).toContainEqual(expect.objectContaining({ from: '../shared', to: 'shared' }));\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:38:        expect(config.extraResources).toEqual([{ from: '.env', to: '.env' }]);\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:41:    it('selects a certificate-store identity only when configured', () => {\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:55:    it('uses the default timestamp server unless an override is configured', () => {\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:62:        expect(() => createBuilderConfig({ publisherName: 'Example Publisher' })).toThrow('Missing signing identity');\ndesktop\\packaging\\builder_config.test.mjs:63:        expect(() => createBuilderConfig({ certificateSha1: 'ABC123' })).not.toThrow();\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:3:title: config service initialized during component render\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:14:`ensureConfigServiceInitialized()` is called in the render body of `ProjectWorkspace` and `ConfigPage`. That is a side effect during render, against the documented two-phase service lifecycle (\"Config-dependent work runs in init()/start()/app bootstrap\"), and fragile under React StrictMode double-rendering and future concurrent rendering.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:17:- Initialize `configService` exactly once in app bootstrap: `useAppBootstrap` already calls `configService.init(...)` — make that unconditional and early (before any component that might read config renders), including the no-last-project path.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:18:- Delete both `ensureConfigServiceInitialized` helpers; components assume an initialized service and fail loudly otherwise (the service already throws).\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:19:- `ConfigPage`'s `useState(() => configService.loadDraft())` initializer also mutates service state during render — move draft loading into a `useEffect` (or an explicit open handler) with state set afterwards.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:22:- No component calls `configService.init` or `loadDraft` during render.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:25:- Existing config tests still pass; a test asserts init happens once during bootstrap.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_016_config_init_during_render.md:29:- `design\\feature_descriptions\\F_016_config.md`\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_018_card_creation_feature_only.md:14:The new-card form in `ProjectWorkspace` hardcodes `type: 'feature'` and the button reads \"Create Feature\"